  "scope": "# Review: 44d20451ce17 destination-edge prototype follow-up\n\nTask/source: `44d20451ce17`; selected generator SHA-256 `ff9c89eb7fe655b851f32e1e273ad9065bab4f3fa8eb3d383bb973e2714869b0`; canonical rule hash `fc96c07b50d8`.\nDefect \u2192 repair: the retained prototype emitted one query and public names exposed fixed seed/setting order; it now emits four distinct queries and names files by SHA-256 of exact visible bytes.\nScope: task-local parametric prototype, focused tests, public examples, design/readme, and current notes only; production `generator.py` and canonical Racket are unchanged.\nEvidence: `checks/parametric/destination-edge-v2-evidence.json` records two fixed-setting episodes, each with 3 demonstrations + 4 queries and seven distinct inputs.\nLabels: all 14 episode labels were executed by the included Racket bridge and match the independent Python parity mirror.\nTeaching: demonstrations distinguish the opposite setting, and every one of the four queries changes under that rival in both episodes.\nPublic projection: two opaque content IDs are sorted, duplicate visible payloads are rejected, query answers/private metadata are absent, and each challenge-file hash equals its ID.\nChecks: focused regression 7/7 and staged task-local suite 83/83; the direct raw `pytest` path remains an import-harness diagnostic, not a generator failure.\nRemaining limit: two values and two retained seeds do not prove all-seed teachability, variant approval, or training admission; no unrelated production battery was run.\nAssessment: main repair is routine and complete in its bounded scope; supplementary peer finding `079232b060cd` needs maintainer attention.",
